// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHY THIS BLOCK IS AT THE FOOT AND NOT THE HEAD
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Two constraints collide at the top of a Pine file and only this placement
// satisfies both:
//
//   1. `//@version=6` MUST be the first line. Pine's compiler directive is
//      positional; pushed down by a licence header the script would be read as
//      an older dialect, and a fixture that no longer round-trips to TradingView
//      is worse than one with an unconventional licence position.
//
//   2. LINE NUMBERS MUST NOT MOVE. This file is the authority for every
//      "line N" reference in `docs/pine/linemap-*.md` and in the owner's own
//      instructions — the tuple `request.security` is line 259 and must stay
//      line 259. A prepended header shifts every reference in the project by
//      its own height, silently.
//
// So the body above is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the script as its author wrote it, and
// `manifest.json` records the hash of that body separately from the hash of this
// whole file, so a re-attached revision is detectable while this block is not
// mistaken for one.
// ============================================================================
